{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"frobenius-reciprocity","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Frobenius Reciprocity"}]},"title_text":"Frobenius Reciprocity","kind":"theorem","taxon":null,"url":"frobenius-reciprocity.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","frobenius-reciprocity"],["kind","theorem"],["label","Theorem"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Let "},{"Math":{"src":"f : X -> Y"}},{"Text":" in a locally cartesian closed category, "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" over "},{"Math":{"src":"X"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"S"}},{"Text":" over "},{"Math":{"src":"Y"}},{"Text":". The change of base adjoints satisfy"}]},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(f) (A × f^* S) ≅ (scripts(∑)_(f) A) × S"}},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∏)_(f) (f^* S =>\nA) ≅ S => scripts(∏)_(f) A"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The first is the "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"Frobenius property"}]},{"Text":" of the coproducts "},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(f)"}},{"Text":" ("},{"Cite":{"key":"jacobs-1999","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":", Lemma 1.9.12)."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Strong":[{"Text":"Proof."}]},{"Text":" For the second, a map "},{"Math":{"src":"T -> scripts(∏)_(f) (f^* S => A)"}},{"Text":" corresponds to a map "},{"Math":{"src":"f^* T × f^* S -> A"}},{"Text":", that is (as "},{"Math":{"src":"f^*"}},{"Text":" preserves products) to a map "},{"Math":{"src":"f^* (T × S) -> A"}},{"Text":", hence to "},{"Math":{"src":"T × S ->\nscripts(∏)_(f) A"}},{"Text":" and so to "},{"Math":{"src":"T -> S => scripts(∏)_(f) A"}},{"Text":". Both sides therefore represent the same presheaf, and are isomorphic by the Yoneda lemma (compare "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"universal-property","label":null,"body":null}},{"Text":"). The first follows the same way: a map "},{"Math":{"src":"(scripts(∑)_(f) A) × S -> T"}},{"Text":" corresponds to "},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(f) A -> S => T"}},{"Text":", to "},{"Math":{"src":"A -> f^* (S => T)"}},{"Text":", to "},{"Math":{"src":"A -> f^* S => f^* T"}},{"Text":" (as "},{"Math":{"src":"f^*"}},{"Text":" preserves exponentials), to "},{"Math":{"src":"A × f^* S -> f^* T"}},{"Text":" and so to "},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(f) (A × f^* S) -> T"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Strong":[{"Text":"For families."}]},{"Text":" In families of types both are direct calculations. At "},{"Math":{"src":"y : Y"}},{"Text":" the left side of the first is"}]},{"Math":{"src":"∑_(x : X) (f x = y) × A thin x × S thin (f x)"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"and transporting along "},{"Math":{"src":"f x = y"}},{"Text":" replaces "},{"Math":{"src":"S thin (f x)"}},{"Text":" by "},{"Math":{"src":"S thin y"}},{"Text":", which no longer depends on "},{"Math":{"src":"x"}},{"Text":" and leaves the sum. Similarly"}]},{"Math":{"src":"∏_(x :\nX) (f x = y) -> S thin (f x) -> A thin x ≅ S thin y -> ∏_(x : X) (f\nx = y) -> A thin x ."}}]}}}]}}
